# Generated artifacts that are committed on purpose but should not be read as review surface.
#
# `openapi.json` and `crates/api-client/src/lib.rs` are ~1 MB of `utoipa` → `progenitor` output
# in a repository whose hand-written source is a fraction of that (BUILD_AND_OPS §9.3), and
# `xtask openapi --check` is what guarantees they match the code — so a reviewer reading their
# diff is reading the same information twice, at length.
#
# `-diff` suppresses the diff body, not the fact that the file changed: `git diff --stat` and
# GitHub's file list still show it, and `git diff --text` still prints it when someone genuinely
# wants to look. `linguist-generated` keeps them out of language statistics and collapses them
# in pull requests.
#
# `Cargo.lock` keeps `linguist-generated` but *not* `-diff`: a lockfile change is exactly what a
# reviewer should be reading, since it is how a dependency actually enters the build.
openapi.json                 linguist-generated=true -diff
crates/api-client/src/lib.rs linguist-generated=true -diff
.sqlx/*.json                 linguist-generated=true -diff
Cargo.lock                   linguist-generated=true

# The repository is developed on Windows and built on Linux. Normalise line endings in the
# index so a checkout on either platform produces the same content hash, and keep the shell
# scripts and Dockerfiles LF whatever the developer's `core.autocrlf` says — a CRLF shebang
# line is a container that fails to start with `no such file or directory`, naming a file that
# is plainly there.
* text=auto
*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile*   text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
